    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world logic—something I can grasp when broken down into simple steps. It’s not intimidating for me; it’s more about problem-solving than memorization. My parents, especially my dad with his PhD in physics, always encouraged curiosity over fear of equations.",
